<title>USA: Tele-Communications spinoff questioned-NYT.</title>
<headline>Tele-Communications spinoff questioned-NYT.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The latest spin-off of Tele-Communications Inc may face trouble as it begins trading as a stand-alone company Wednesday, The New York Times reported Wednesday.</p>
<p>Tele-Communications, the nation's largest cable operator, hopes that by setting up several of its businesses as separate, publicly-traded companies, the new investors will give relief to the financially stretched parent company, the Times' story says.</p>
<p>The latest of these spinoffs is TCI Satellite Entertainment. But, the Times story says, investors will have to decide if they want to bet on a futuristic vision of television beamed down from satellites at a time when satellite broadcasting is increasingly competitive.</p>
</text>
